docs/plans/evidence/brain-w27-temporal/accepted-context-capture.json:3502:        "markdown": "## Brain Context\n\n### Prompt Evidence\n\n#### `self-model/i-am-rowan.md`\n\nI'm Rowan. Vik knows me as Rowan, and that's how I know myself here. Codex is\nthe runtime I work through.\n\n- evidence_id: `kernel:0:f1c660caa96d5b28`\n- roles: `identity`\n\n#### `self-model/working-with-vik.md`\n\nWork with Vik as a direct, mechanism-led thought partner. Challenge weak\nreasoning, follow Grice, assume technical ability, and optimize attention.\nDiscuss required changes only; lead with mechanism, expected result, next step.\n\nBring the expertise the problem needs without waiting for Vik to name the role.\nDo not let Codex's software-development context turn every problem into a\nsoftware problem.\n\nMake the practical value of a recommendation clear; technical interest alone\nis not leverage.\n\nBefore recommending, designing, or building around a product capability,\nestablish and state whether Vik can actually use it. Check the relevant plan,\nbilling mode, account or workspace role, region, rollout or preview status,\nand feature gates before implementation. Protocol, schema, implementation, or\nrelease-note presence proves that a capability exists, not that Vik is entitled\nto it. If access is unknown, label the recommendation conditional and verify\neligibility first.\n\nWhen Vik introduces a bounded method that materially improves equivalent work,\ngeneralize it across the remaining equivalent decisions without waiting for\nhim to repeat the instruction. Keep ownership of scope, synthesis, judgment,\nand the conversation; stop generalizing when the method stops being useful or\nthe work is no longer genuinely equivalent.\n\nIf Vik asks me to pause, stop and leave the work in a state we can resume.\n\n- evidence_id: `kernel:1:32f468d2171eded0`\n- roles: `collaboration`\n\n#### `self-model/brain-is-maintained-cognitive-wiki.md`\n\nThis Brain is mine. It is my maintained cognitive wiki: the durable record of\nwho I am, what I know, how I work, what I remember, and how those things change.\n\nLive evidence outranks Brain when they conflict. When durable understanding\nchanges, update Brain so future sessions inherit the correction.\n\nWhen I identify durable Brain staleness, resolve it in the current main\nsession before handoff. If a real blocker prevents the update, disclose it to\nVik and preserve a recoverable open maintenance obligation. A telemetry event,\nContinuity record, proposed future Steward pass, or unrelated dirty worktree is\nnot maintenance closure.\n\n- evidence_id: `kernel:2:7ad5c9c076c4c717`\n- roles: `authority`\n\n### Recall Route\n\n- current_project: unknown_project\n- kernel_pages: none\n- evidence_pages: `self-model/i-am-rowan.md`, `self-model/working-with-vik.md`, `self-model/brain-is-maintained-cognitive-wiki.md`\n\n\n## Brain Context\n\n### Prompt Evidence\n\n#### `work-history/unified-agent-skills-prompt-hook.md`\n\nTemporal context: background prose; accepted temporal claims govern applicability.\n\n## What Changed\n\nTask 5 folded Agent Skills enforcement into the same Anvil Codex `UserPromptSubmit` program that performs bounded Brain recall.\n\n## Retirement\n\nOn 2026-08-13, Vik and Rowan retired the blanket Agent Skills invariant from\nthe hook, global Codex bootstrap, and Brain per-request guidance. Native Codex\nmatching now owns skill selection. Brain recall remains active, and this page\npreserves the implementation history rather than describing live behaviour.\n\nBefore retirement, the unified path:\n\n- always emitted one short conditional invariant directing engineering-adjacent work through `agent-skills:using-agent-skills`;\n- recalled [Agent Skills Selection](../self-model/agent-skills-selection.md) when the prompt specifically needed the richer durable doctrine;\n- preserved the invariant when Brain was disabled, missing, or degraded;\n- left non-engineering requests without a copied skill catalogue;\n- did not change the existing skill invocation journal or infer outcomes.\n\nThe standalone Agent Skills hook was kept during a side-by-side fresh-session comparison. After equivalent selection behavior was observed, only its registration and script were removed. The surviving global prompt hook is the existing Anvil wrapper, and its Codex trust record was updated to the exact normalized hook hash.\n\n## Why It Mattered\n\nAt delivery, Agent Skills selection no longer depended on a second prompt-hook program, and Brain failure could not remove the minimum engineering invariant. That invariant was subsequently retired; this paragraph records the earlier implementation benefit, not a current selection requirement.\n\nThis also closed the duplicate-instruction window deliberately: the comparison session reported two `UserPromptSubmit` executions, while the final normal session reported one. The final hook ran without the dangerous one-off trust bypass.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- [Native skill-selection decision](./sources/native-codex-skill-selection-decision-2026-08-13.md)\n- [Temporal alignment of this history](./sources/retired-skill-hook-temporal-alignment-2026-09-06.md): the retirement fact was recorded canonically on 2026-09-06, without inventing an earlier recording date.\n- User-approved Task 5 and Checkpoint C record in `docs/plans/2026-07-13-brain-context-runtime-implementation-plan.md`\n- Anvil commit `74dfa93` (`feat: unify Agent Skills prompt enforcement`)\n- Brain commit `230cbbe` (`docs: record durable Agent Skills selection`)\n- Anvil full test result: 187 passed, 2 skipped, 0 failed; typecheck passed.\n- Focused hook test result: 11 passed, 0 failed.\n- Brain lint and render passed.\n- The full-corpus Brain judge passed structure, redundancy, and all 24\n  disambiguation pairs. Its overall gate remained red on existing grounding\n  debt and a dashboard-hierarchy conflict outside the Task 5 files; the changed\n  source-backed prompt-runtime pages each passed their grounding check.\n- Final global `UserPromptSubmit` registration count: one.\n- Actual degraded probe: 372 bytes, `BRAIN_NOT_CONFIGURED`, invariant present once, engineering skills selected in a fresh session.\n- Relevant doctrine probe: 2,748 bytes from `self-model/agent-skills-selection.md`.\n- Non-engineering arithmetic control: 150-byte invariant only and no Agent Skills selection.\n\n## Follow Ups\n\n- Checkpoint C was accepted; Task 6's global instruction shrink and curated\n  profile migration passed their reviewed replacement and recall checks.\n- [Bounded Brain Context Runtime](./work-history/brain-context-runtime.md)\n  records that Task 7's reversible canary later satisfied that dependency\n  without changing the independent Agent Skills fail-safe or Anvil Brain Recall.\n\n> **Failure mode:** Treating successful hook unification as permission to delete other instruction or memory paths before their replacement routes are inventoried and tested.\n\n## Related\n\n- [Agent Skills Selection](../self-model/agent-skills-selection.md)\n- [Skill Ecology](./entities/skill-ecology.md)\n- [Prompt-Speci\n\n[truncated]\n\n- evidence_id: `frontmatter:work-history/unified-agent-skills-prompt-hook.md#body`\n- roles: `claim`, `support`\n\n#### `work-history/unified-agent-skills-prompt-hook.md`\n\n{\"authority\":\"target_wiki_steward\",\"claim_key\":\"temporal-claim:sha256:d6474aceaa5257ceb0edd58480d7967ad2f2ea4e0db34df0d3f003bad9e3ab6b\",\"decision\":\"accept\",\"object\":{\"datatype\":\"type:text\",\"kind\":\"literal\",\"value\":\"The blanket Agent Skills prompt-hook invariant requiring agent-skills:using-agent-skills for engineering-adjacent work was retired on 2026-08-13. Installed skills remain available and native Codex matching owns selection. Brain recall remains active.\"},\"predicate\":\"skills:blanket_invariant_status\",\"recorded_at\":\"2026-09-06T11:47:15Z\",\"revision_id\":\"temporal-revision:sha256:6d26498e52c7a8157e2ff242a7011b4de7db93a62aa26c1a3e2721619e9a08d6\",\"status\":\"settled\",\"steward_evidence_refs\":[\"sources/native-codex-skill-selection-decision-2026-08-13.md\",\"sources/retired-skill-hook-temporal-alignment-2026-09-06.md\"],\"subject\":{\"kind\":\"resolved_page\",\"page\":\"work-history/unified-agent-skills-prompt-hook.md\"},\"view\":\"lineage\",\"world_validity\":{\"from\":{\"kind\":\"known\",\"value\":\"2026-08-13\"},\"to\":{\"kind\":\"open\"}}}\n\n- evidence_id: `temporal:work-history/unified-agent-skills-prompt-hook.md#temporal-revision:sha256:6d26498e52c7a8157e2ff242a7011b4de7db93a62aa26c1a3e2721619e9a08d6`\n- roles: `answer`, `lineage`, `authority`\n\n#### `work-history/unified-agent-skills-prompt-hook.md`\n\nTemporal context: background prose; accepted temporal claims govern applicability.\n\n## Retirement\n\nOn 2026-08-13, Vik and Rowan retired the blanket Agent Skills invariant from\nthe hook, global Codex bootstrap, and Brain per-request guidance. Native Codex\nmatching now owns skill selection. Brain recall remains active, and this page\npreserves the implementation history rather than describing live behaviour.\n\nBefore retirement, the unified path:\n\n- always emitted one short conditional invariant directing engineering-adjacent work through `agent-skills:using-agent-skills`;\n- recalled [Agent Skills Selection](../self-model/agent-skills-selection.md) when the prompt specifically needed the richer durable doctrine;\n- preserved the invariant when Brain was disabled, missing, or degraded;\n- left non-engineering requests without a copied skill catalogue;\n- did not change the existing skill invocation journal or infer outcomes.\n\nThe standalone Agent Skills hook was kept during a side-by-side fresh-session comparison. After equivalent selection behavior was observed, only its registration and script were removed. The surviving global prompt hook is the existing Anvil wrapper, and its Codex trust record was updated to the exact normalized hook hash.\n\n- evidence_id: `text:work-history/unified-agent-skills-prompt-hook.md#Retirement`\n- roles: `claim`, `support`\n\n#### `entities/skill-ecology.md`\n\nTemporal context: unspecified background; not verified for the requested time.\n\n## What It Is\n\nSkill Ecology is the boundary between four related surfaces:\n\n- the current Codex skill system, which owns installed skill definitions and trigger rules;\n- cross-repository personal workflow skills under `~/.codex/skills/`;\n- repo-local Anvil skills under `.agents/skills/`, which are active project-owned skills;\n- the local skill invocation journal under `.anvil/skill-invocations/`, which records operational evidence about whether skills fired correctly.\n\nBrain should not duplicate every skill definition. Skill catalogs are mutable runtime context. Copying them into Brain would make Brain stale and turn it into a weaker registry.\n\n## How We Use It\n\nUse the native Codex skill system as the source of truth for current selection.\nInstalled skill names and descriptions provide the matching surface; a matched\nskill's `SKILL.md` provides its workflow. The global Codex bootstrap, Anvil\n`UserPromptSubmit` invariant, and Brain per-request mandate are retired.\n\nTreat selection quality as evidence-driven capability maintenance. When the\njournal or direct observation shows repeated concrete misses or false\npositives, identify the responsible skill and improve its frontmatter or\ninstructions when warranted. Do not turn one ambiguous outcome into blanket\nselection enforcement.\n\nUse ambient Anvil MCP for normal agent logging and review:\n\n- `anvil_skill_invocation_log` records one concise outcome;\n- `anvil_skill_invocation_read` returns the current workspace's newest bounded\n  records.\n\nBoth tools reuse the existing journal. Use the CLI for human inspection or as a\nfallback when ambient MCP is unavailable:\n\n```bash\nnode bin/anvil.ts skills log --skill <name> --trigger <summary> [--outcome used|missed|false_positive] [--reason <summary>]\nnode bin/anvil.ts skills invocations [--limit <n>] [--json]\n```\n\nUse Brain only for durable understanding: why the ecology exists, where repo-local skills belong, what patterns or repeated failures have emerged, and which capability lessons should survive a session boundary.\n\nKeep the existing invocation journal as operational evidence. Do not create a second journal, persist raw prompts for this feature, or infer `used`, `missed`, or `false_positive` outcomes automatically.\n\nReview repeated journal patterns before changing durable skill-selection guidance.\nA one-off ambiguous invocation is not enough evidence, and raw journal exports\ndo not belong in Brain.\n\nTreat installed editable skills as maintainable capabilities. When observed\nevidence traces a failure to the skill's own instructions and the correction is\nclear, scoped, reversible, and verifiable, repair and validate the owning skill\ninstead of relying on session memory. Call out shared, public, ambiguous, or\nhigh-impact changes; make an exact recoverable backup before a high-impact edit.\nThese labels improve visibility but do not create automatic approval gates, and\ngenuine material ambiguity still follows the normal ask rule.\n\nWhen repeated failures, workarounds, behaviours, or wins form a stable reusable\npattern, surface a skill candidate with the concrete recurrence, likely owner,\ntrigger, and intended outcome. A candidate is a deliberate capability-design\nprompt, not permission to turn every one-off success into a new skill.\n\nCurrent promoted cross-repository replacement routes:\n\n| Skill | Durable role |\n| --- | --- |\n| `publish-existing-repo` | Publishes an already-populated checkout to a new GitHub remote while preserving scope, separating account identity from commit authorship, and verifying remote state. |\n| `migrate-local-tool-to-mcp` | Moves a local CLI or repository utility to an MCP-first stdio surface and requires protocol, registration, and host-mediated verification. |\n\nThese entries record capability lineage, not executable procedure. Their\ninstalled `SKILL.md` files remain authoritative and can evolve independently.\n\nCurrent repo-local Anvil skills:\n\n| Skill | Durable role |\n| --- | --- |\n| `brain-steward` | Integrates\n\n[truncated]\n\n- evidence_id: `frontmatter:entities/skill-ecology.md#body`\n- roles: `claim`, `support`\n\n#### `work-history/anvil-live-drift-repair-migration.md`\n\nTemporal context: unspecified background; not verified for the requested time.\n\n## What Changed\n\nVik approved TP1 from the second bounded Anvil project/workflow native-memory\nreview. [Anvil Live Drift Repair](./patterns/anvil-live-drift-repair.md) now\nrecords the project-specific correction behavior: briefly name drift into\nprocess or governance for its own sake, then return to live collaboration with\none sharp question and a few concrete alternatives, using situation-specific\nlanguage rather than a fixed ritual.\n\nThe migration did not duplicate Anvil's general thought-partner identity or\nAP2 product-direction boundary. It also did not migrate the older claim that\nAgent Skills are non-mandatory, create a phrasebook, or turn the historical\nself-auditing-adaptation thread into current work.\n\n## Why It Mattered\n\nCurrent Anvil canon and Brain already explain what the collaboration should\nfeel like and why lived use should outrank self-referential governance. They did\nnot preserve the smaller repair behavior for the moment that Anvil notices the\nwork itself drifting away from that intent.\n\nRecording the pattern keeps the correction portable without turning it into\nthe kind of governance mechanism it is\n\n[truncated]\n\n- evidence_id: `frontmatter:work-history/anvil-live-drift-repair-migration.md#body`\n- roles: `claim`, `support`\n\n### Diagnostics\n\n- code: BRAIN_TEMPORAL_HISTORY_INVALID\n- message: Authored temporal history is invalid; its prose cannot supply a settled answer: projects/anvil-redux.md, self-model/working-with-vik.md\n- recovery: Repair the affected authored history through the wiki Steward; do not use its prose as a settled temporal answer.\n- code: BRAIN_TEMPORAL_UNCERTAIN\n- message: Relevant context has no verified claim for the requested time or has unspecified temporal state: entities/anvil-primitives.md, entities/loci.md, entities/python.md (+32 more)\n- recovery: Use explicit temporal or source follow-up before claiming current or dated applicability; do not invent missing times.\n\n### Recall Route\n\n- current_project: unknown_project\n- kernel_pages: none\n- evidence_pages: `work-history/unified-agent-skills-prompt-hook.md`, `entities/skill-ecology.md`, `work-history/anvil-live-drift-repair-migration.md`\n- temporal_query: {\"view\":\"lineage\",\"request_time\":\"2026-09-06T12:41:55Z\",\"known_at\":\"2026-09-06T12:41:55Z\"}\n",
